description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts, in the region "A slice sequence cut short by a capacity refusal never got its attempt either", deliver a reach verdict after the slice compose call so its execution row can be graded.

REGION. Ground on the comment beginning "A slice sequence cut short by a capacity refusal never got its attempt either", which occurs exactly once in this file. Above it, inside the slice loop, is an invocation of resolveFeatureCompose assigned to sliceCompose, followed by the line that assigns its body to lastBody. That assignment is the edit site.

THE DEFECT, measured by census. This file invokes resolveFeatureCompose at three separate call sites and verdict delivery currently exists at only one of them. Counted on the live substrate over the thirteen compose executions since delivery landed: every one logged a successful trace capture, so every report carried the execution identifier, yet only two rows ever received a reach tag, and delivery coverage on new rows has fallen from twenty nine percent to fifteen percent as more executions pass through the unpatched paths. Their verdicts are never sent and their rows stay permanently ungraded. This is the same defect class as the original: an identifier that exists and is discarded because a sibling call site was missed.

WHAT MAKES THIS SAFE. Both halves are in scope at the insertion point: the slice report carries the trace store's execution identifier on its execution_id field, and the verdict is its ok field. This mirrors the delivery already present at the first call site. It is fire and forget with a bounded timeout and a swallowing catch, so a trace-store problem cannot affect the slice result, and the loop's control flow and every downstream read of lastBody are untouched.

Perform exactly one replacement. Find the sole occurrence of this line:
      lastBody = sliceCompose.body as Record<string, unknown>;

Replace it with these lines:
      lastBody = sliceCompose.body as Record<string, unknown>;
      try {
        const reachId3 = typeof lastBody["execution_id"] === "string" ? (lastBody["execution_id"] as string) : "";
        if (reachId3.length > 0) {
          const reachEndpoint3 = process.env["METABOB_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8080";
          const reachKey3 = process.env["METABOB_API_KEY"] ?? "";
          void fetch(`${reachEndpoint3}/v2/activities/execution-traces/reach`, {
            method: "POST",
            headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", ...(reachKey3 ? { Authorization: `ApiKey ${reachKey3}` } : {}) },
            body: JSON.stringify({ execution_id: reachId3, reached: lastBody["ok"] === true }),
            signal: AbortSignal.timeout(5000),
          }).catch(() => { /* grading must never affect the slice result */ });
        }
      } catch { /* verdict delivery is best effort */ }

The first line is reproduced verbatim so every downstream read of lastBody is unchanged, including the verdict checks immediately below it. Distinct local names are used so this cannot collide with the delivery blocks at the other call sites. No imports are added: fetch is global and the API key is already read from the environment elsewhere in this file.

One replacement, one file, inside the named region. Change nothing else.

